#%PAM-1.0
# The PAM stack greetd uses for the greeter's *own* session (the `greeter`
# account running cage + ionix-greeter). greetd looks for this service first and
# only falls back to `greetd` when it is missing.
#
# It exists so the greeter does not share the user login stack: ionix-post-install
# adds pam_gnome_keyring to /etc/pam.d/greetd to unlock the keyring with the
# login password, and without this file the greeter account went through it too,
# starting a keyring daemon with no home (`unable to create keyring dir:
# /.local/share/keyrings`). This is greetd's stock stack, keyring-free.
auth       required     pam_securetty.so
auth       requisite    pam_nologin.so
auth       include      system-local-login
account    include      system-local-login
session    include      system-local-login
